    <!-- TAB 0: KEY WORDS -->
    <div class="tab-content active">
        <div class="card">
            <div class="intention"><strong>Today:</strong> you'll tell the story of the great network of routes that linked China to the Mediterranean for over a thousand years — and you'll master the passive voice, the structure English uses to describe what <em>was carried, was traded and was spread</em> when the doer matters less than the deed.</div>

            <div class="note" style="border-left:4px solid #764ba2;">
                <strong>Warm up — a few words worth carrying with you.</strong> Each one comes from an earlier story in this series. <strong>Met it before?</strong> Say what it means and use it in a sentence of your own. <strong>New to you?</strong> Even better — it's a useful word to add today. Reveal to check.
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent"><b>a voyage</b><br>What does it mean? Use it about a long journey.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a voyage</b> (n) — a long journey, especially by sea.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent"><b>an empire</b><br>What does it mean? Name one empire from history.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>an empire</b> (n) — a large group of lands or peoples ruled by a single state or leader.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent"><b>a merchant</b><br>What does it mean? Use it about someone who buys and sells goods.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a merchant</b> (n) — a person whose business is buying and selling goods, often over long distances.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent"><b>to flourish</b><br>What does it mean? Use it about a city or a business that did well.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>to flourish</b> (v) — to grow strongly and successfully; to thrive.</div>
            </div>

            <h2>Now — the words for today's story</h2>
            <p>Each new word is hidden in a sentence. <strong>Read it aloud and say what you think the bold word means</strong> from the rest of the sentence — then reveal it and see how close you were.</p>

            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">1. Rather than one highway, the Silk Road was a vast <b>lattice</b> of connected roads, mountain passes and sea lanes reaching across the whole of Asia.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a lattice</b> (n) — an interlaced, criss-crossing web of many connecting lines, routes or parts.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">2. A long line of camels, a <b>caravan</b> loaded with bales of cloth and sacks of spice, moved slowly across the desert from one town to the next.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a caravan</b> (n) — a group of traders and pack animals travelling together across difficult country.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">3. Every valuable cargo of silk and jade counted as a precious <b>commodity</b> — something bought and sold for a high price in distant markets.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a commodity</b> (n) — a raw material or product that can be bought and sold; a good that is traded.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">4. Traders rarely crossed the whole distance; goods were passed from hand to hand as <b>intermediaries</b> in each city bought them and sold them onward.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>an intermediary</b> (n) — a middleman; someone who stands between two sides and helps goods or messages pass between them.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">5. An <b>oasis</b> town, green with water in a sea of sand, gave exhausted caravans a place to rest, drink and trade before the next stretch of desert.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>an oasis</b> (n) — a fertile, watered place in a desert where plants grow and travellers can stop.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">6. Chinese silk-makers guarded their <b>monopoly</b> jealously: for centuries, they alone knew the secret, so they alone could sell the cloth.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a monopoly</b> (n) — complete control of the supply of a good, so that no one else can provide it.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">7. Ideas travelled as easily as goods; along the same roads whole religions were <b>disseminated</b> from one land to another, carried in the words of merchants and monks.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>to disseminate</b> (v) — to spread or scatter something, especially ideas, knowledge or beliefs, widely.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">8. Where different peoples met and mixed, a rich <b>confluence</b> of languages, art and technology took place in the busy market squares.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a confluence</b> (n) — a flowing together; the merging of different peoples, cultures or streams of ideas in one place.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">9. The same routes that carried wealth also carried a deadly <b>plague</b>, a disease that swept along the trade lines and killed millions.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>a plague</b> (n) — a fast-spreading, often deadly disease that affects very large numbers of people.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="guess-item">
                <div class="sent">10. The whole system depended on <b>diplomacy</b> — patient talks and agreements between empires that kept the roads open and the traders safe.</div>
                <button class="reveal-btn" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('show')">Reveal</button>
                <div class="meaning"><b>diplomacy</b> (n) — the art of managing relations between states through discussion and agreement rather than war.</div>
            </div>

            <h3>Now use them — out loud</h3>
            <div class="discuss">
                <strong>Talk it through before we read:</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>Using <em>lattice</em>, <em>caravan</em>, <em>commodity</em> and <em>confluence</em>, predict: what kind of things do you think travelled along these routes?</li>
